xnu 0180: publish the GMU HFI power tables and hold the GX rail

FW_INIT_RESULT=0x100 and CORE_FW_START prove the CM3 runs, but without the
PERF (id 4) and BW (id 3) tables the GMU does not know the SM8475 OPPs, and
without the default vote (id 30) it never applies them. Port the same
PongAdrenoPower tables: read the gfx/mx/cx level and SH0/MC0/ACV bandwidth
resources from the cmd-db, build the 58-word PERF and 159-word BW payloads,
send them, then CORE_FW_START and the default vote, and finally the oob_gpu
hold. The GMU ACKs every message with err 0, the default vote reports
gpu 2 / bus 2, and the GX GDSCR reads PWR_ON=1. The CPU-side GDSC sequence
stays as a fallback; gmustart=1 and gpugx=1 still gate the new path.
